      "redditQuotes": [
        {
          "text": "The underwater waterfall at Le Morne Brabant, Mauritius — it's an optical illusion caused by sand and silt being driven off the shelf. Absolutely surreal to see from above.",
          "source": "r/CantBelieveThatsReal · Underwater waterfall post (high upvotes)",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.reddit.com/r/CantBelieveThatsReal/"
        }
      ],
      "insiderTip": "Manage expectations — this is more of an atmospheric experience than a great reef snorkel. You won't see the \"waterfall\" from water level. But the edge where shallow meets deep is genuinely eerie and beautiful, and the sand formations below are mesmerizing. Combine with a Crystal Rock stop on the same boat trip.",
